  "question": {
    "text": "Equivalent conductivity at infinite dilution for $\\quad$ sodium-potassium oxalate $\\left[\\left(\\mathrm{COO}^{-}\\right)_{2} \\mathrm{Na}^{+} \\mathrm{K}^{+}\\right]$ will be [given molar\r\nconductivities of oxalate, $\\mathrm{K}^{+}$ and $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$ ions at infinite dilution are $148.2, \\quad 50.1,$ $73.5 \\mathrm{S} \\mathrm{cm}^{2} \\mathrm{mol}^{-1}$ respectively $]$",
    "image": null
